[Music]  welcome to iowa where wind turbines rule  the land  and in the town of esterville there is a  wind program dishing out some of the  best wind technicians in the country  i'm joel caulfield and i'm here with my  dad jim caulfield we are students at  iowa lakes community college and we're  studying to be wind turbine technicians  [Music]  this is iowa lakes community college a  school that offers an intensive two-year  program in applied science in wind  turbine technology  jim and his son joel are students who  enter the program together  a wind technician is somebody who would  actually work on the wind turbine to  make sure that it is being serviced  properly and if it breaks down actually  be able to repair it you just basically  take a variations of different  electrical theory classes all the way up  to advanced level stuff of actual wiring  up circuits and advanced programming of  computers  wind turbine is actually big pieces of  equipment that carry a lot of risk and  that's why they are engraining in us  everything we need to know so that when  we're up there we know how to handle  every situation we can deal with  when you're going out to the turbine for  the first time you're very anxious and  nervous because you're going at a height  that you're never been to before  i mean there's a lot of fall potential  that could happen  to elaborate on what joel's saying it's  serious stuff that you don't take  lightly at all  when you get to the top you just start  to get more of an excitement over fear  and exhaustion because now you're up  there in the cell itself so it's  actually kind of cool to see a working  turbine in first action  for jim and joel going back to school  was a no-brainer jim left the trucking  industry after 26 years to follow his  passion in renewable energy and his son  joel wanted to travel the world and work  with his hands so enrolling in the win  program at the same time while  unconventional ended up working out  perfectly  we can bounce off each other for ideas  and stuff like that help each other with  like homework so it kind of gave us an  opportunity to grow better  there's a lot of things that i'm still  scratching my head on and you know he'll  just come by and it's like well you got  to do this and you've got to how do you  know that how do you know what he does  he gets it  it's actually a great feeling knowing  that i have a chance to  you know pursue a career in something  that i've been very passionate about  there are other people doing this and  it's worth it for anybody to go ahead  and make that next leap  [Music]

